Sustainable transportation systems minimize environmental impacts while delivering products efficiently through low-emission modes and optimized logistics networks. Design choices like product weight, size, packaging, and shipment consolidation directly influence transportation emissions and feasibility of sustainable logistics options. By designing for efficient transportation, companies reduce embodied carbon, lower logistics costs, and enable greater use of rail, sea, and other low-emission modes. Sustainable transportation also supports last-mile solutions like cargo bikes and pedestrian delivery in urban areas, reducing congestion and emissions.